The error indicates that the `BuildServiceProvider` extension method is not found, which usually comes from the `Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection` namespace. This suggests the test project might not have the necessary package or using directive.

To work around this, I will create a minimal mock `IServiceProvider` implementation to test the `GetStoreOptions` method instead of using a real DI container. This will allow us to control the `GetService<IEmbeddingGenerator>` call and test the behavior of the method that calls `GetService`.

I will submit a test file that mocks `IServiceProvider` and tests the `GetStoreOptions` method via reflection, covering the call to `GetService` on `IServiceProvider`.

